{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\froman\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}\f0\fs24 DocuSign Envelope ID: d4e5f607-8192-4a3b-a0c1-4e5f6a7b8c9d\par 1. Agreement\par This Confidentiality Agreement is made between Theta Logistics, LLC ("Company") and AlphaCorp Holdings, Inc. ("Counterparty"). The parties wish to explore a business opportunity and may exchange confidential information for that purpose.\par 2. Confidential Information\par "Confidential Information" means all information disclosed by one party to the other, in any form, whether or not marked or identified as confidential, relating to the disclosing party's business, products, customers, finances, or technology.\par 3. Exceptions\par The obligations in this Agreement do not apply to information that: (a) is or becomes publicly known through no fault of the receiving party; (b) was lawfully in the receiving party's possession before disclosure; (c) is lawfully obtained from a third party without restriction; or (d) was independently developed by the receiving party without reference to or use of the disclosing party's Confidential Information.\par 4. Use of Confidential Information\par The receiving party shall use Confidential Information only to evaluate the business opportunity described above.\par 5. Protection\par The receiving party shall protect Confidential Information using the same degree of care it uses to protect its own confidential information, and in no event less than reasonable care.\par 6. Disclosure to Personnel\par The receiving party may disclose Confidential Information to its employees who need to know it for the permitted use and who are subject to written confidentiality obligations.\par 7. Required Disclosure\par The receiving party may disclose Confidential Information to the extent required by law, regulation, or court order, provided that it gives the disclosing party prompt written notice where legally permitted and discloses only the portion legally required.\par 8. Term\par This Agreement begins on the date of last signature and remains in effect for two (2) years.\par 9. Survival\par The confidentiality obligations in this Agreement continue for three (3) years from the date of disclosure.\par 10. Return of Materials\par On written request, the receiving party shall promptly return or destroy all Confidential Information and all copies of it.\par 11. No License\par Nothing in this Agreement grants any license or right under any intellectual property of the disclosing party.\par 12. No Warranty\par Confidential Information is provided without warranty of any kind as to accuracy or completeness.\par 13. Equitable Relief\par The parties agree that a breach of this Agreement may cause irreparable harm and that the non-breaching party may seek injunctive relief.\par 14. No Commitment\par This Agreement does not obligate either party to enter into any further agreement or transaction.\par 15. Governing Law\par This Agreement is governed by the laws of the State of California.\par 16. Venue\par The parties submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal courts located in San Francisco, California.\par 17. Assignment\par Neither party may assign this Agreement without the prior written consent of the other party.\par 18. Notices\par All notices must be in writing and delivered to the addresses set out below the signature blocks.\par 19. Entire Agreement\par This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement of the parties regarding its subject matter and may be amended only in a writing signed by both parties.\par 20. Severability\par If any provision is held invalid, the remaining provisions remain in effect.\par 21. Counterparts\par This Agreement may be signed in counterparts, each of which is deemed an original.\par IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the parties have executed this Agreement as of the date first written above.\par AlphaCorp Holdings, Inc.\par By: /s/ Dana Reyes\par Name: Dana Reyes\par Title: Vice President, Legal\par Theta Logistics, LLC\par By: /s/ Morgan Ellery\par Name: Morgan Ellery\par Title: General Counsel\par }